{"name":"New Orleans","slug":"new-orleans","region":"North America","lat":29.95,"lon":-90.07,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb temperatures in New Orleans show no clear long-term trend. There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run cooler, and El Niño accounts for about 10% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 90% of a normal year-to-year swing. Without El Niño, a Dec–Feb this cool would come about once every 5 years. El Niño moves the hottest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about -1.6 °C, against 0.7 °C for the coldest days. Dec–Feb rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a wetter season with more rainy days and more intense heavy-rain days, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. Humidity shows no clear trend or El Niño link. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a cooler-than-normal season is more likely than not (about 60%), about 1 °C below the 1991–2020 average; a wetter-than-normal season is likely (about 95% chance). The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":13.4357,"trend_per_decade":0.1105,"trend_p":0.125,"trend_total_since_1951":0.8288,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.4467,"enso_p":0.009,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.0911,"intrinsic_sd":1.3224,"effect_this_season":-1.13,"effect_ratio":0.8546,"size":"Substantial","size_typical_el_nino":"Substantial","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":5,"expected_anomaly_2027":-1.0287,"forecast_mean":12.407,"forecast_sd":1.4366,"p_below":0.6183,"p_near":0.2733,"p_above":0.1084,"forecast_words":"More likely than not (62%): a cooler-than-normal season","within_record":false,"trend_part_2027":0.1014,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.2126,"trend_p":0.0593,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2792,"enso_p":0.2936,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.7065,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.0467,"trend_p":0.6107,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.5173,"enso_p":0.0135,"confidence":"Clear","shift_this_season":-1.3088,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.1142,"trend_p":0.1113,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.6328,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":-1.6011,"lines_cross":false},"tails":{"enso_difference":-0.9121,"enso_difference_p":0.0015,"trend_difference":-0.0983,"trend_difference_p":0.3958}},"values":[13.098,15.652,13.493,13.764,13.103,13.635,16.109,10.997,12.128,11.745,11.844,13.964,10.95,10.427,13.486,12.088,12.491,11.983,12.499,11.237,13.746,15.651,12.506,15.152,14.762,12.885,10.523,9.821,11.645,12.931,11.303,12.698,12.825,11.067,12.684,12.664,12.117,12.44,14.447,12.882,13.93,13.557,14.172,12.289,13.546,12.68,13.533,12.919,15.045,