t push is about 90% of a normal year-to-year swing. Without El Niño, a Mar–May this cool would come about once every 5 years. Mar–May rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño may have an effect toward a wetter season, though the evidence is thin, and this year's shift is substantial. Humidity shows no clear trend or El Niño link. For Mar–May 2027, a cooler-than-normal season is slightly favored (about 45%), about 0.2 °C below the 1991–2020 average; a wetter-than-normal season is likely (about 70% chance), resting on an El Niño effect that is not clearly established. The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":20.7273,"trend_per_decade":0.1652,"trend_p":0.0003,"trend_total_since_1951":1.2387,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.2715,"enso_p":0.0089,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.0912,"intrinsic_sd":0.8032,"effect_this_season":-0.6869,"effect_ratio":0.8552,"size":"Substantial","size_typical_el_nino":"Substantial","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":5,"expected_anomaly_2027":-0.2497,"forecast_mean":20.4776,"forecast_sd":0.8727,"p_below":0.4362,"p_near":0.3017,"p_above":0.262,"forecast_words":"Slightly favored (44%): a cooler-than-normal season","within_record":false,"trend_part_2027":0.4373,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":-41.5933,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.2612,"trend_p":0.0142,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.3868,"enso_p":0.1632,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":-0.9787,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.1479,"trend_p":0.0021,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.3513,"enso_p":0.0003,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":-0.8887,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per